    "/apis/v1/booking/rates": {
      "post": {
        "description": "Booking Hotel Rates\n\nThis operation returns what the page at `url` shows when it is fetched. Currency, language and regional content are decided by the rendered page and the location it is fetched from, not by your URL: URL parameters that select them (for example a currency or language parameter) may be ignored. Read the currency and locale values in the response instead of assuming the ones in your URL.\n\nStay dates are those of the rendered page. Compare `data.rates[].arrival_date` and `data.rates[].los` (number of nights) with the dates in your URL before using the rates.",
